      "content": "Your perspective aligns with historical consensus, as critics often framed union opposition as a threat to free market capitalism and corporate freedom, yet the reality was a genuine struggle for better working conditions and democratic power in the face of exploitation. While some anti-union rhetoric was inflated to discredit legitimate demands for fair treatment, the broader economic arguments about \"efficiency\" and \"cost\" became justifications for policies that systematically weakened organizing power over time. Whether one views these tactics as genuine economic concerns or political tools to protect profits is partly a matter of interpretation, but the core goal of unions in securing federal protections for the middle class remains an undeniable fact.",
